WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:06.730
Speaker 1: OK, I have received dozens of emails
and tweets and comments asking me to weigh

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.690
in about what's currently happening with the
online left.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.980
As many of you know, I really don't watch
much online political media.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.560
I limit myself to the stuff I read to be ready
to do the show.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.090
And then I have other interests in limited
time each day.

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:24.930
But I am sort of aware of a bunch of the different
things that have been going on with the online

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:25.930
left.

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:29.260
And I want to talk about it a little bit because
I do think that it's actually there's a lot

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:30.260
to say here.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:34.500
Now, as I understand it, there's a few different
controversies happening right now.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:40.930
I am very much aware of young Turks host Jank
Ugur and also young Turks host Anna Kasparian

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:45.740
embroiled in again, if I understand it correctly,
it's a couple of different controversies.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:51.020
One is specifically related to another host
named Jimmy Daw and sexual harassment or harassment,

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:52.610
as some like to say.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:57.610
And then another kind of more general controversy
is between Genk and the Young Turks and a

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:03.130
sort of contingent of the authoritarian revolutionary
left that has a presence online, people like

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:04.239
Glenn Greenwald and others.

00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:06.860
I'm not exactly sure who else is part of this.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:09.900
And so a few things are going on there.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:14.600
And then on the other hand, it seems as though
there was kind of a shake up at the hills

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:17.420
rising and there are new hosts there.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:20.960
And that seems to be going pretty poorly from
the one one thing I read about it and the

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:25.180
question I've basically been getting from
people in the audience is whether the online

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:30.890
left is tearing itself apart in a way that
is counterproductive to the progressive movement

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:34.640
and whether the left has become overrun with
with with grifter's.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:36.900
So let's take these questions one at a time.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:42.230
And I want to say I was actually just interviewed
for a podcast by Cliff Schecter and John Aravosis,

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:43.930
where we talk quite a bit about this.

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:46.630
And we're going to publish this over the weekend.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:49.409
And we talk a lot about this issue.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:54.340
If the topic interests you, there's, you know,
probably 20 minutes of this stuff in that

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:56.810
episode which will publish to our YouTube
channel.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:02:03.110
So first of all, the fact that there are different
views on the left is not bad.

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:04.880
It's not a source for concern.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:09.189
And it's always been my perspective that diversity
of opinion is fine and good and should be

00:02:09.189 --> 00:02:11.079
applauded and welcomed.

00:02:11.079 --> 00:02:15.870
What has been a concern for me has been the
increased gatekeeping that I've seen some

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:20.829
on the left and Gagin, which includes call
outs about who really is or isn't on the left.

00:02:20.829 --> 00:02:25.529
I've received many of those as well as kind
of shaming people for views and generally

00:02:25.529 --> 00:02:29.840
unproductive insults when somebody doesn't
line up one hundred percent with your political

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.599
perspective, generally speaking, diversity
of opinion is good.

00:02:33.599 --> 00:02:35.459
It's not a problem in and of itself.

00:02:35.459 --> 00:02:39.909
What is a problem is when people start to
focus merely on calling out others, either

00:02:39.909 --> 00:02:44.959
for personal reasons or for clicks or for
money or to keep or to virtue signal or for

00:02:44.959 --> 00:02:46.349
whatever reason they do it.

00:02:46.349 --> 00:02:48.219
So I'm going to give you an example.

00:02:48.219 --> 00:02:53.390
When Jimmy Door has attacked me, he did on
Twitter during the election period last year,

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:58.829
I've mentioned my views differ from Jimmy
Dorce, but I don't base my show in my identity

00:02:58.829 --> 00:03:04.459
around calling out people like Jimmy Daw with
whom I have differences of opinion.

00:03:04.459 --> 00:03:05.889
First of all, it just seems so boring.

00:03:05.889 --> 00:03:08.010
Secondly, it's so childish.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:10.769
Third, what would I even get from doing that?

00:03:10.769 --> 00:03:12.309
It would probably be profitable.

00:03:12.309 --> 00:03:16.609
And I've jokingly talked with others about
who should I start a fake beef with because

00:03:16.609 --> 00:03:19.019
it gets attention, but it's just not me.

00:03:19.019 --> 00:03:21.329
It's not productive in any in any real sense.

00:03:21.329 --> 00:03:25.279
Now, the issue of grifter's is a complicated
one.

00:03:25.279 --> 00:03:31.370
And when I say grifter, what I mean is someone
is creating a persona and covering stories

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:35.689
or taking positions or covering stories in
a way that doesn't represent who they really

00:03:35.689 --> 00:03:41.650
are either because they've decided I can concoct
this persona and appeal to a certain audience

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:43.879
or it's going to be profitable in some way.

00:03:43.879 --> 00:03:46.430
I might get paid speaking gigs or whatever
the case may be.

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:48.510
Now, here's what I can say about that.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:53.090
I'm going to give you a list of people that
I know are not grifters.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:57.950
And what I mean by that is whether we agree
or disagree on any particular issue.

00:03:57.950 --> 00:04:03.280
What you see them say publicly lines up completely
with what they say privately.

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:05.260
They are not playing characters.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:09.099
They're not calculating their positions for
how it's going to be perceived by their audiences

00:04:09.099 --> 00:04:10.950
or for profitability.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:16.630
And the reason I'm able to give you this list
is because I know both these people's public

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:22.380
work as well as knowing them privately as
individuals and in no particular order.

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:27.940
Here are people that are not Grifter's, Genk
and Anna from the Young Turks.

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:29.440
I've known them both for a long time.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:34.410
If you talk to them privately, what they say
is exactly what they say on their show.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:36.440
We don't have to agree about everything.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:40.760
Surely I'd have differences with them about,
for example, the Israeli-Palestinian conflict,

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:44.880
but they are totally sincere in what they
say and what they believe would be best for

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:45.880
the world.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:47.930
I am totally sincere in what I say.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:50.660
There is no grift or calculation there.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:51.660
Great.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:57.120
OK, Sam Ceder from the majority report I've
been to what must be at this point 15 or 20

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:00.680
conferences with Sam over the years where
we spend hours together.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:05.390
Every political conversation I've had with
Sam and that I've heard and overheard Sam

00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:10.390
have with other folks, including people from
the Revolutionary Left, etc., the public,

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:13.650
Sam and the private Sam is exactly the same
person.

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:14.660
No grift.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:16.130
Kyle Kolinsky.

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:21.450
I've hung out with Kyle and I've talked to
Kyle Atun over the years, the Kyle you see

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:23.680
on his YouTube channel, as far as I know.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:26.430
And again, I don't watch a lot of this stuff
online.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:29.430
It's the same Kyle that I know privately.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:36.290
Faran Cousins from Ring of Fire is the same
guy politically, privately as he is publicly.

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:37.290
No.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:42.080
Mickey from The Namiki Show, I've known her
for probably a decade.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:45.990
Private Namiki and Public Namiki are the same
person.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:49.920
This is not someone who I guess we traditionally
consider to be on the left in this.

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:52.180
I don't know how my audience will react to
this.

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:58.340
Joe Rogan, whatever your problems are with
the things Rogan says, and I recently did

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:01.400
a video where I said I disagree with what
Joe is saying about vaccination.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.510
I think he's mistaken.

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:04.900
There is no act there.

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:11.010
I can tell you, Rogan, five minutes before
the show starts and an hour after and on the

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:13.120
show, it's it's the real Rogen.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:18.891
OK, now, anybody outside of this list, some
of them are grifters, but many of them, I

00:06:18.891 --> 00:06:19.990
just don't know privately.

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:25.610
So I can't really say I don't know well enough
to say their public persona is different than

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:28.420
the person they are in private, either for
profit or not.

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:31.550
Some I don't want to name names because then
I'm just engaging in the same stuff.

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:33.990
But there are plenty of grifters.

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:37.000
So then the question is, is the grifting going
to tear the left apart?

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.260
But probably not.

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:45.280
Some people will make money and are making
money with the grifting, with the calculated

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:46.840
fake personas.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:51.860
There are others who will then make money
from attacking the grifters and on and on.

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:53.360
It's not really my thing.

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:59.070
I don't think it's particularly good for the
progressive movement to have people with retrograde

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:02.310
ideologies passing themselves as being on
the left.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:08.620
You know, if you are an authoritarian or a
faux populist or you defend or sympathize

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:13.750
the authoritarians or the faux populists and
the dictators and the strongmen, I would question

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:16.100
whether you're really on the left.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:22.270
It's not a left I recognize, but I don't know
that it's really going to tear the left apart.

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:24.930
A lot of these movements seem way bigger.

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:29.050
If you look at Twitter and Reddit and YouTube,
then they really are.

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:31.210
But it's going to continue being profitable.

00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:33.070
So it's going to continue.

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:34.790
That's basically my take.

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:36.470
And a lot of it is very boring.

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:39.940
A lot of it is extraordinarily childish.

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:44.190
And the unfortunate reality is that to some
degree.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:49.740
We're all slightly narcissistic, and what
I mean by that is anybody who I mean, OK,

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:53.370
if you're neuro divergent, then this this
may not apply, OK?

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:59.230
But for people who are, you know, not autistic
and you decide, I'm going to have a show where

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:03.110
I give my opinion, there's some degree of
narcissism there.

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:09.400
There has to be because somewhere you believe
that your opinion may be as opposed to or

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:15.270
different than millions and millions and millions
of people who never occurs to do a show.

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:19.920
Your opinion is of some value entertainment
or it's something that other people would

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:20.920
want to listen to.

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:25.900
So you're going to have a lot of interesting
and different personalities in this space.

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:29.650
But within that, there's a huge, huge spectrum.

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:35.149
And by its nature, you're going to get this
this stuff within the space.

00:08:35.149 --> 00:08:40.909
And I think that there are aspects of it that
aren't good for the progressive movement,

00:08:40.909 --> 00:08:45.670
but I don't think it's ultimately going to
be destructive in the way that some believe

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:51.220
it's going to be, because much of the survival
of this very space, the online left, depends

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:54.040
on conflict and depends on controversy.

00:08:54.040 --> 00:09:00.839
And so the idea that it will become a distraction
from policy, sure, but it's not going to destroy

00:09:00.839 --> 00:09:02.330
the space overall.

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:04.029
We'll have more of this on our Instagram.

00:09:04.029 --> 00:09:07.139
You can follow us on Instagram at David Pakman
show.

00:09:07.139 --> 00:10:24.560
And I'd love to hear your thoughts as well.

